3 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/8a/f8/cd/ce/5344483d5575cd8c/dscn0264_original.jpg?hash=0cd62042eac13a1a73a8509959f928a425467f4311d6c62e94a410ebcf6101d4.1795075199
3 FORM jpg
3 TITL Folketelling 1762 Følling i Stod Vanderaas
3 NOTE 5. 5. Ingeborg? No,  as far as I can see by skimming speedily through the records right now we don't have her name as Ingeborg in the primary sources we have included here . Where did you see the name Ingeborg for Haagens wife?
3 NOTE 3. d.y. = "den yngre"  = the younger.  As opposed to "d.e." = den eldre = the elder. It's the same as  in English. Meaning there was an older relative, i.e the father or a grandfather having the same name. 
3 NOTE 3. Moe is surely also a place name. 
3 NOTE 2. The children mentioned with other place names ar grown ups. When the record was made they were in working age and had moved away from their parents, maybe they had even got their own home or farm and a full family.
3 NOTE 1. The last name Vanderaas is also a place/farm. It could be this one:
4 CONT https://www.google.no/maps/place/Vander%C3%A5sen/@64.0844529,11.4336319,11z/data=!4m2!3m1!1s0x4672902644adaac1:0x2a3592b2e4927a56
4 CONT I don't at present have any historical maps at hand  to  get more sure. Today there is also another place called Vanderås in the same region:
4 CONT https://www.google.no/maps/place/Vander%C3%A5s/@63.6986642,11.028362,10.46z/data=!4m2!3m1!1s0x466d65f8702d88ab:0x878fdaf707319800
3 NOTE I am new to diving into my Norwegian side, so if anyone can answer these questions, I'd be so grateful. Based on the information below the photo:
4 CONT 1. Where did the last name of "Vanderaas" come from? Why were they not simply Haagensen/datter?
4 CONT 2. I see some children had other last names, such as Holtan and Klæbu. Those are places, so I figure they added them as last names for that reason? Is this correct?
4 CONT 3. Why would Rasmus have the last name of "Moe" if he was simply a farmer for, I assume, a person "Moe"? (I tried to find a village of the name but couldnt so assumed it was a person)
4 CONT 4. What does the "d.y'" stand for after Ander's name?
4 CONT 5. I see Gollaug is the wife, but I thought her name in other records was Ingeborg. 
4 CONT
4 CONT Ok, I think that's all the questions I have for this! Thank you in advance for helping me to understand some of these customs.
