2 TITL The first Danish sea voyage to the South of Africa
1 NOTE Olai Ovenstad: Militµrbiografier. Norske hµroffic. 1628-1814. 1948
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT F°rste kommandant pσ Akershus
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT Ove Giedde var en framstσende man. Sedan Dansk Ostindisk Compagni bildats 1616, ledde han endast 24 σr gammal en expedition med fem fartyg, som Christian IV 1618 sΣnde ut f÷r att upprΣtta handelsf÷rbindelser med Ostindien. Efter e
2 CONC tt bes÷k pσ Ceylon anlΣnde flottan 1620 till Indiens syd÷stkust. HΣr f÷rhandlade Giedde med den tamilske fursten i Tanjore och kunde pσ Christian IV:s vΣgnar sluta avtal om handelsrΣttigheter och ÷vertagande av en liten fiske- och
2 CONC  handelsplats. Detta blev inledningen till 225 σrs innehav av Trankebar, som var Danmarks f÷rsta utomeuropeiska besittning. 1620 pσb÷rjades dtillfσngatogs av svenskarna under kriget 1658 och avled samma σr som Tomarp ÷vergick i sv
2 CONC ensk Σgo. Pσ honom syftar ett i Skσne f÷rr vΣlkΣnt ordstΣv, som omtalas i Gustaf Ljunggrens "Skσnska Herregσrdar": "det Σr ude med Ove Giedde". Det gσr tillbaka till berΣttelsen om en bonde, som sett Ove Giedde i sina galonerade k
2 CONC lΣder sitta och Σta sallad och som vid hemkomsten berΣttat: "nu Σr det ude med Ove Giedde, han Σder grΣs og stopper sine klΣder med halm".
2 CONT ____________________
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT Denmark had 3 major colonies:
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT *The Koromandel Coast in India with trade stations in the Bengal, Java, Borneo and Celebes.
2 CONT *The Guinea Coast (200 kilometres of it!) in West Africa.
2 CONT *The Virgin Islands (3 islands) in the Caribbean Sea in America.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT Beside trading posts and colonies, Denmark had a trading post in Canton in China, just like the big-
2 CONT ger colonial powers.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT The triangle Denmark-Africa-West Indies created many fortunes in Copenhagen as well as did the silk route from China
2 CONT It all started in 1618, when the Danish King Christian the 4th equipped a fleet that should sail to In-
2 CONT dia and establish a Danish trading post on the way to China. The commander was Ove Giedde, a 24
2 CONT years old nobleman, and the fleet consisted of 2 naval ships ELEFANTEN ("The Elephant") and
2 CONT DAVID and two merchant ships KI╪BENHAVN ("Copenhagen") and CHRISTIAN. In March
2 CONT 1618 the first ship, the yacht ╪RESUND ("The Sound") commanded by the Dutchman Roland
2 CONT Crappe, left Copenhagen, and shortly after that the main fleet set sail.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT At the same time another explorer, commander Jens Munk, got the kings permission to try to find a
2 CONT passage north of the Americas to China, and he left 19th of May same year with two naval vessels,
2 CONT the frigate ENHI╪RNINGEN ("The Unicorn") and the yacht LAMPRENEN ("The Lamprey"). His mission failed, and he returned with only two survivors two years later.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT The Indian fleet had lots of problems. A mutiny in January 1619 in the Channel. On 19th
2 CONT of February the fleet took 2 pirate ships at Cap Verde and included them in the fleet. At the same time, the
2 CONT chief merchant, a Dutchman named Boshouwer was exposed as a fraud. By the time the fleet got to
2 CONT South Africa over 200 men had been lost and during the next 9 months, when the fleet sailed along
2 CONT the African east coast to India, another 100 men died.
2 CONT <br />
2 CONT Ove Gjedde, the commander, got a part of the coastline Trinquemale on Ceylon from the King of
2 CONT Candy on 21st of August 1620. This was not a nice piece of land, so eventually he went to the
2 CONT Coromandel Coast in the Tanjore Province, where his second in command Roland Crappe had been
2 CONT awarded some land of his old friend the Naik at a place called Tarangambadi. European name was
2 CONT Trankebar. On the 16th of October that year the first customs pay 16 thaler was paid to the Dan-
2 CONT ish authority. Denmark kept the "colony" for 200 years.
