2 NOTE Peder Als (b. Copenhagen 1726, d. s.p. 1776)
3 CONT
3 CONT A pair of portraits of Colonel Christian Ulrich von Sundt (1720–1775), and his wife Benedicte Rudolphine von Ingenhaeff (1735–1803). He in a powdered wig, wearing a cuirass under a red uniform jacket. His left hand is resting on a
3 CONC  helmet and a fur-lined cape is draped over his right arm. She in a powdered wig, wearing a blue silk dress with lace sleeves and collar under a fur-lined red velvet cape draped over her right shoulder. Her hair, neckline and slee
3 CONC ves are adorned with large pearls. Unsigned. Later inscribed on the reverse. He: Oil on canvas. She: Oil on canvas laid on cardboard. C. 77×63 cm each. Period frames. (2).
3 CONT
3 CONT Provenance: Bruun Rasmussen auction 567, 1991 no. 9, reproduced pp. 18–19. Bruun Rasmussen auction 658, 1999 no. 291, reproduced pp. 128–129.
2 NOTE Portrait by Peder Als (b. Copenhagen 1726, d. s.p. 1776).
